## 6️⃣ Putting it all together – a reusable “greeting service” class (pseudo‑code)

```pseudo
class GreetingService:
    def __init__(self, geo_provider, country_lang_map, lang_greeting_map, default="Hello"):
        self.geo = geo_provider                # e.g. MaxMindReader or API wrapper
        self.c2l = country_lang_map
        self.l2g = lang_greeting_map
        self.default = default
        self.cache = LRUCache(maxsize=5000, ttl=300)   # 5 min

    def get_greeting(self, ip):
        # 1️⃣ Cache check
        if ip in self.cache:
            return self.cache[ip]

        # 2️⃣ Resolve country
        country = self.geo.country_for_ip(ip)   # returns ISO‑2 or None
        if not country:
            greeting = self.default
        else:
            # 3️⃣ Language lookup
            lang = self.c2l.get(country.upper())
            # 4️⃣ Greeting lookup
            greeting = self.l2g.get(lang, self.default)

        # 5️⃣ Store & return
        self.cache[ip] = greeting
        return greeting
```

You can instantiate it once at app start‑up and call `service.get_greeting(request_ip)` wherever you need a greeting.

